          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "えんりょする — enryo suru — \"to hold back; to decline politely\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "あたまが いたいので、おさけは えんりょします。 — atama ga itai node, osake wa enryo shimasu — \"My head hurts, so I will say no to the sake.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Polite えんりょします, enryoshimasu; a する verb. Past (polite): きゃくは えんりょしました。, kyaku wa enryo shimashita."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "えんりょする (enryo suru) is built from a Sino-Japanese noun and the native verb suru, \"to do\". The noun, enryo, is two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese: en, \"far\" (Middle Chinese hjwonX) and ryo, \"thought\" (ljoH) (KANJIDIC2; JMdict; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
